### Keep tray setup running when theme monitoring fails

**Severity:** `medium`

`ThemeListener` starts WMI watchers and can throw when theme monitoring is unavailable. This new construction runs during `FrmScreen_Load` before cursor setup and `UpdateNotifyIcon()`, so letting the exception reach the outer catch skips the rest of that initialization.

Catch and log construction failure locally, then return so the caller continues with the currently selected icon.

```suggestion
            try
            {
                themeListener = new ManagedCommon.ThemeListener();
            }
            catch (Exception e)
            {
                Logger.Log(e);
                return;
            }
```
